I've had baby dragons attack shopkeepers.  The shopkeeper will usually
be able to kill one, but if there are two or more s/he's doomed and I
get much stuff, gold, and a skeleton key without losing telepathy (and
whatever else you lose when you destroy a shopkeeper while you're in
human form).
>When they're both full grown, pop on a ring of conflict and let them
>fight to the death; stand nearby so you can cover the corpse of the
>loser before the winner eats him.  Now eat the loser's corpse to pick 
>up Disintegration resistance - a very nice thing to have before you
>meet any wild black dragons.  Possible problems with all of this
>include falling down a level and not getting back in time before your
>tame dragons go wild...
>
Do baby dragons hatched from eggs you lay fight you if you leave them
alone for too long?  I know this happens for "normal" pets.  I've left
a baby dragon alone on another level for quite some time and when I
returned it was still tame.


